                <pb facs="0591" n="503" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg503"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gummeré to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-06-23"><hi rendition="#italic">June 23,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Gummeré acknowledges receipt of Department’s instructions yesterday, and
                    states that, while acting in close touch with the British minister, he has not
                    entertained any idea of departing from his present <pb facs="0592" n="504"
                        xml:id="pg504"/> attitude without having first received positive
                    instructions from the Department. He reports that Shereef left for Zellal’s
                    village very early this morning with money and prisoners.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
